DATA

  Lichess 2017 game sample
    Originally published by "datasnaek" on Kaggle under CC0 1.0 (public domain
    dedication). Retrieved via the GitHub mirror at ogreowl/chess-analysis.
    Contains games played on lichess.org.

  The Week In Chess (TWIC)
    PGN issues 210-1649 retrieved from the rozim/ChessData GitHub mirror. TWIC
    is compiled and published by Mark Crowther (https://theweekinchess.com).
    From 2020 the coverage is majority online blitz; chess-lab infers format
    from Event and Site headers and restricts classical analyses accordingly.
    The moves of a chess game are facts and are not subject to copyright;
    compilations and accompanying editorial content may be. This repository
    stores no TWIC text or annotations, redistributes no PGN files, and uses
    only the move sequences and standard result/rating/date tags for
    statistical analysis. Users fetching this data should respect TWIC's terms.

  chess.com Titled Tuesday exports
    Retrieved via github.com/ianrastall/titled-tuesday-archive, which publishes
    chess.com's event exports renamed and sorted, under an MIT licence
    (Copyright (c) 2026 ianrastall). The underlying game records are chess.com's
    exports, and game scores themselves are facts. A
    pinned one-in-five sample of events (data/titled_tuesday_events.txt) is
    fetched at build time and is not redistributed. Only move sequences, results,
    final clock times, time controls and FIDE identifiers are used.

  lichess-org/chess-openings
    ECO opening classification tables, CC0 1.0.

ENGINE EVALUATIONS
  data/eval/ contains Stockfish evaluations of the games above, produced by
  this project. They are chess-lab's own output and are distributed under the
  same Apache-2.0 terms as the code.

No third-party data files are redistributed in this repository. scripts/fetch_data.sh
retrieves them from their upstream sources at build time.
